/*  commentProbe -- CAN A COMMENT LIVE IN A DIRECTIVE STORE AND LAND IN THE .mm ONLY?

    The feasibility probe docs/commentDirectives.md is gated on. It applies ONE comment to the
    generated GroupRules.mm, anchored on a `// slug` line, with a BLOCK-comment payload.

    ⚠ THE ANCHOR IS THE SLUG TOKEN ALONE, and for two independent reasons that agree:
    Clay's -- the sentence half of `// slug sentence?` is optional and gets edited, so matching
    the whole line orphans every comment under it; and the standing one -- a fromThis may not
    contain `//` or a quote, because checkSkip swallows comment-shaped text even inside a quoted
    value. Two reasons, one spelling.

    ⚠ THE PAYLOAD IS A BLOCK COMMENT for the same standing reason: a `//` cannot be written into
    a kant value today. That is the constraint that decides whether this store is buildable now
    or waits for checkSKIP, and it is what this probe is for.

    ⚠ IT EDITS A GENERATED FILE AND closeFile WRITES IT BACK. The undo is `tok GroupRules.twk`,
    which is also the idempotency mechanism: the retok discards the insert, so applying again
    lands the same bytes. Do NOT run it twice without a retok between -- the comment doubles,
    because insertAt has no already-present check.  */
Start();
include(directives);

register(Directives);
define
    source="GroupRules.mm";
    cp01 source fromThis="ruleDoorSeat" toThis="\t/*  commentProbe: this line came from a directive store, not from the twk  */\n" where=after;
    ;

getFile(source);
insertAt(cp01);
closeFile(source);

cerr "COMMENTPROBE SENTINEL":;
stop();
